Title: Obsidian Protocol
Credit: Written by
Author: A. Writer
Draft date: 2026-09-29

===

INT. OBSIDIAN SAFE-HOUSE - NIGHT

The room breathes with industrial silence. A single amber practical
hangs overhead, its weak cone of light refusing to reach the walls.

VIKTOR enters through the heavy steel door, scanning the room with
the calibrated patience of a man who has learned that hurry kills.

He crosses to the tactical map spread across the folding table.

VIKTOR
We've been compromised.

                    (beat)

Every cell. Every safe-house within the network.

IVAN (O.S.)
How many are exposed?

Viktor traces a finger along the map, stopping at three circled
locations.

VIKTOR
All of them.

He kills the overhead light. The room collapses into monitor glow.

EXT. ROOFTOP - CONTINUOUS

Rain hammers the cityscape below. AGENT SORINA crouches behind
a ventilation unit, earpiece alive with static.

SORINA
(into earpiece)
Package is secure. But Viktor knows.

She peers over the edge. Thirty stories down, a black SUV idles.

SORINA (CONT'D)
He's moving the asset tonight.

INT. BLACK SUV - NIGHT

Viktor sits in silence. The city streaks past in neon blurs.

DRIVER
Where?

Viktor's reflection watches him from the rain-streaked window.
He does not answer immediately.

VIKTOR
Somewhere they haven't mapped yet.

INT. UNDERGROUND GARAGE - NIGHT

Fluorescent strips flicker above rows of concrete pillars.

Viktor steps out of the vehicle and walks into the dark with
absolute certainty.
